# rsync exclude patterns for the public snapshot.
#
# actions/checkout only materializes tracked files, so anything already in .gitignore will
# not be present anyway. Listing those paths here regardless is deliberate: it makes the
# filter correct when run locally against a dirty working tree, and it survives a file being
# accidentally committed later.
#
# Patterns are rsync filter rules, not gitignore rules. A trailing / matches directories
# only; a leading / anchors to the repo root.

# Never publish VCS or CI-local state
.git/
.github/public-README.md

# Agent state. Three of these skills carry the domain and the LAN prefix in their scaffolding
# examples, and unlike manifests they are never substituted -- postBuild only reaches the
# kustomize build output. Excluding the directory is simpler and more durable than editing
# them, since a future skill would reintroduce the problem silently.
.claude/

# Editor state
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Extra needles for scripts/public-gate.sh. Kept out of the mirror because the values it
# checks for are exactly the values that must not be published -- a gate that names them in
# its own source defeats itself. The script works without this file.
.publicgate-extra

# Local Coder CLI state. .coder/pprof is a unix socket, which rsync cannot copy and warns
# about noisily.
.coder/

# Local Terraform provider and module cache under the Coder templates. Not present in CI,
# where checkout only materializes tracked files, but a local dry run copies a few hundred
# MB of provider binaries without this and tells you nothing useful.
.terraform/

# Internal planning notes. These discuss the cluster's real addresses, the hostname inventory
# and this publishing effort itself. They are working documents, not portfolio material.
docs/plans/
